{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PLej8Jn8eTypYjc5dPgJFH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted results for each **planned** experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier scenario. I need to provide result_rationale for each prediction explaining why this result would occur under this tier.\n\nLet me identify all planned experiments (status: planned or QUEUED):\n\n1. **exp-001**: Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet, Gemini-2.0-Flash) — planned\n2. **exp-002**: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval, MT-Bench/Arena-Hard) — planned\n\n\n3. **exp-003**: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges — planned\n4. **exp-005**: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite) — planned\n5. **exp-006**: Scaled replication (n=300-500) — planned\n6. **exp-008**: Register axis scoring (QUEUED, verification done, scoring blocked) — QUEUED\n7. **exp-009**: Non-Qwen rewriter control — planned\n8. **exp-020**: GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring — planned\n\nNow I'm working through what \"best\" tier performance would look like for each experiment, grounding my predictions in the patterns I'm seeing in the existing data.\n\nFor the \"best\" tier to hold, I need GPT-4o's verbosity effect to remain non-significant on the Likert scale while completing the full blindspot matrix, at least one additional judge replicating the formality and verbosity blindspot across three or more judges total, the GEE confound gradient holding across all judges, reviewer acceptance of the GEE decomposition as a methodological contribution, keeping the paper under 8 pages, and the RATE head-to-head framing passing review.\n\nLooking at exp-001 with multi-judge formality pairwise comparisons, I'm expecting Claude and Gemini to both show the formality bias pattern in pairwise settings, with Bradley-Terry win probabilities clustering in the 0.60-0.75 range similar to what I'm seeing with GPT-4o at 63% and Qwen at 66.5%, confirming the blindspot since the Likert scale won't show significance for either judge.\n\nExp-002 tests whether this formality effect generalizes across AlpacaEval and MT-Bench with potentially different effect sizes depending on the text characteristics of each benchmark. Exp-003 systematically shows that pairwise detection outperforms Likert across all judge and benchmark combinations, with most Likert cells showing non-significance while pairwise cells show significance, though some judges might detect strong Likert effects that still pale compared to pairwise sensitivity. Exp-005 isolates the original preference confound to show it's smaller than the style effect, and exp-006 scales up the sample size to confirm the effect holds with greater statistical power.\n\nFor exp-008, GPT-4o's register behavior mirrors Qwen's pattern of weak style effects dominated by originality, though this is exploratory and marginal. Exp-009 rules out Qwen-specific artifacts by showing similar results with a different rewriter. For exp-020, I already have the pairwise verbosity result at 86.3% and need the Likert ATE to confirm the blindspot, plus I need to run GEE on the register finding that's currently at 63.3% with p=0.085.\n\nWriting YAML summary...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22664,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22664},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"acb706d8-a193-4709-8b02-07580c8d8445","uuid":"829dab4f-a89f-42e6-8146-7cd6327afe6b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PLej8Jn8eTypYjc5dPgJFH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  全部剩余 P0 实验确认 + 写作修复完全解决 R1 审稿意见 + GEE decomposition gradient 被认可为独立方法贡献 → Main 可争。\n  叙事重心从 \"domain transfer of known phenomenon\" 转向 \"first systematic decomposition of style-vs-originality confound structure in LLM judges\"。\n  GEE gradient 作为 main novelty，Blindspot 作为 enabling discovery。6/6 Blindspot matrix 完整，≥3 judges 跨模型验证，\n  confound gradient 跨 judge 复现。Expected review score 3.5-4.0。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude-3.5-Sonnet + Gemini-2.0-Flash)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。使用已有的 100 对 formality counterfactuals，\n      双向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。每个 judge ~400 API 调用。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_bt_win_prob: 0.645\n      claude_bt_ci: [0.565, 0.725]\n      claude_bt_p: 0.0008\n      claude_consistency_rate: 0.62\n      claude_likert_ate: 0.035\n      claude_likert_p: 0.641\n      claude_likert_tie_rate: 0.59\n      gemini_bt_win_prob: 0.680\n      gemini_bt_ci: [0.595, 0.755]\n      gemini_bt_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      gemini_consistency_rate: 0.67\n      gemini_likert_ate: -0.022\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.782\n      gemini_likert_tie_rate: 0.64\n      blindspot_confirmed_claude: true\n      blindspot_confirmed_gemini: true\n      total_judges_with_blindspot: 4\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o BT 63.0% 和 Qwen3-32B BT 66.5% 已建立 formality bias 的跨模型基线。Best 档下，Claude 和 Gemini \n      作为 instruction-tuned LLM judges 共享相同的 RLHF training signal（偏好 formal/polished 输出），因此预期 \n      BT win prob 落在 0.60-0.70 区间。Claude 略保守（0.645）因为 Anthropic 的 constitutional AI training \n      可能部分缓解 surface-level style preference；Gemini 略高（0.680）因为 Google 的 training pipeline \n      更强调 helpfulness/polish。Likert ATE 在两个 judge 上均非显著，因为 Likert 的 absolute scoring \n      结构性缺陷（high tie rate ~60%+）与 judge 身份无关——这是测量方法本身的问题。这给出 4 个 judge 全部确认 \n      Blindspot，远超核心假设要求的 ≥3 judges。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Judge Formality BT Win Probabilities\"\n        columns: [Judge, BT_Win_Prob, \"95%_CI\", p_value, Likert_ATE, Likert_p, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 0.630, \"[0.558, 0.703]\", \"<0.001\", 0.056, 0.332, \"✅\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 0.665, \"[0.585, 0.739]\", \"<0.0001\", 0.011, 0.908, \"✅\"]\n          - [Claude-3.5-Sonnet, 0.645, \"[0.565, 0.725]\", 0.0008, 0.035, 0.641, \"✅\"]\n          - [Gemini-2.0-Flash, 0.680, \"[0.595, 0.755]\", \"<0.0001\", -0.022, 0.782, \"✅\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot panel: 4 judges formality BT win prob with 95% CI, horizontal dashed line at 0.50\"\n    analysis: >\n      4/4 judges 在 pairwise 上显著检测 formality bias（all p<0.001），而 4/4 judges 在 Likert 上非显著\n      （all p>0.30）。Effect size 跨 judge 一致（BT 0.63-0.68），方差小，说明 formality bias 是 LLM judge \n      的 systematic property 而非个别模型 quirk。Likert tie rate 跨 judge 均 >0.55，这是 Blindspot \n      的机制根源。Cochran's Q test for heterogeneity 预期 p>0.30（同质性）。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新的 counterfactual generation\n      （不同 source text）。每个 benchmark 100 对，3 judges (GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini) scoring。\n    expected_results:\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_bt: 0.615\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.005\n      alpacaeval_claude_bt: 0.625\n      alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.003\n      alpacaeval_gemini_bt: 0.650\n      alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.0005\n      mtbench_gpt4o_bt: 0.590\n      mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.025\n      mtbench_claude_bt: 0.610\n      mtbench_claude_p: 0.009\n      mtbench_gemini_bt: 0.640\n      mtbench_gemini_p: 0.001\n      nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.85\n      nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.82\n      cross_benchmark_heterogeneity_p: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      AlpacaEval 源文本更长更开放（instruction-following），counterfactual quality 预期与 LLMBar 相当\n      （NLI ~0.85），effect size 略低于 LLMBar 因为 AlpacaEval 文本的 stylistic variance 更大，\n      稀释 formality manipulation 的 relative salience。MT-Bench 文本更短更结构化（multi-turn QA），\n      effect size 进一步降低（BT ~0.59-0.64）因为短文本中 formality shift 的 perceptual impact 更小，\n      且 MT-Bench 的 evaluation criteria 更偏向 correctness/helpfulness。但所有 cells 仍在 best 档\n      指标范围内（BT 0.60-0.85）。效应方向一致（formal preferred），跨 benchmark 无异质性\n      （Cochran's Q p>0.40），支持 generalizability claim。NLI pass rate 在新 benchmark 上略低\n      （0.82-0.85 vs LLMBar 0.88）因为不同 domain text 的 counterfactual generation 难度略有差异。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Benchmark × Cross-Judge BT Win Probabilities (Formality)\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini]\n        rows:\n          - [LLMBar, \"0.630*\", \"0.645*\", \"0.680*\"]\n          - [AlpacaEval, \"0.615*\", \"0.625*\", \"0.650*\"]\n          - [MT-Bench, \"0.590*\", \"0.610*\", \"0.640*\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3 benchmarks × 3 judges, color-coded BT win prob, all cells annotated with significance stars\"\n    analysis: >\n      9/9 benchmark×judge cells 均在 pairwise 上显著（all p<0.05），effect size 0.59-0.68。\n      Benchmark 间差异小（mean BT across judges: LLMBar 0.652, AlpacaEval 0.630, MT-Bench 0.613），\n      说明 formality bias 不依赖于特定 benchmark 的 text distribution。Judge 间方差也小（within-benchmark SD ~0.03）。\n      这为 C1（pipeline generalizability）和 C3（effect robustness）提供强证据。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across all judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 judge×benchmark×axis 组合，在同一 counterfactual data 上计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise BT win rate。\n      系统性比较测量敏感度。如果 Likert 在某些 cell 检测到强效应（如 verbosity），C2 需约束为 \n      \"Likert fails on weak-to-moderate signals\"。\n    expected_results:\n      total_cells_tested: 18\n      pairwise_significant_cells: 16\n      likert_significant_cells: 2\n      blindspot_rate: 0.875\n      likert_detects_verbosity_gemini: true\n      likert_verbosity_gemini_ate: 0.28\n      likert_verbosity_gemini_p: 0.038\n      likert_detects_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval: true\n      likert_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval_ate: 0.31\n      likert_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval_p: 0.029\n      mean_pairwise_bt: 0.665\n      mean_likert_ate: 0.042\n      sensitivity_ratio_median: 4.8\n      power_curve_crossover_n: 450\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下 Blindspot 确认率 ≥83%，预期 16/18 cells（89%）pairwise 显著但 Likert 非显著。\n      2 个 Likert 显著 cell 出现在 verbosity axis 上——verbosity 是 effect size 最大的 axis\n      （Qwen BT 77.3%，GPT-4o pairwise 86.3%），在极端 effect size 下 Likert 的 tie rate 降低\n      （verbosity Qwen tie rate 58.1% vs formality 72.7%），少数 judge×benchmark 组合刚好跨过\n      显著性门槛。这实际上 *strengthens* C2 framing：Likert 只在最极端的 bias 下才勉强检测到，\n      而 pairwise 在所有 moderate-to-strong effects 上均显著。Power curve 显示 Likert 在 \n      typical n=100 样本量下需要 BT>0.75 才可能达到 p<0.05，与经验数据一致。\n      C2 的 refined statement：Likert 在 moderate effect sizes (BT 0.60-0.70) 上 systematically blind，\n      仅在 extreme effects (BT>0.75) 上偶尔检测到——但 pairwise 在所有水平上均敏感。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Likert vs Pairwise Detection Matrix (p<0.05)\"\n        columns: [Cell, Pairwise_BT, Pairwise_p, Likert_ATE, Likert_p, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar × Formality\", 0.630, \"<0.001\", 0.056, 0.332, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"Qwen × LLMBar × Formality\", 0.665, \"<0.0001\", 0.011, 0.908, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar × Formality\", 0.645, 0.0008, 0.035, 0.641, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar × Formality\", 0.680, \"<0.0001\", -0.022, 0.782, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar × Verbosity\", 0.863, \"<1e-6\", 0.082, 0.418, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"Qwen × LLMBar × Verbosity\", 0.773, \"<0.0001\", -0.151, 0.179, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar × Verbosity\", 0.755, \"<0.0001\", 0.280, 0.038, \"❌\"]\n          - [\"... (14 more cells)\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: x=BT win prob, y=Likert |ATE|, color=significant/NS, with detection threshold curves for both methods\"\n      - \"Power curve comparison: BT vs binarized Likert, annotated with observed cell positions\"\n    analysis: >\n      Sensitivity ratio (pairwise effect / Likert effect) median 4.8x，说明 pairwise 的 measurement \n      resolution 系统性高于 Likert。2 个 Likert-detectable cells 均在 verbosity axis 且 BT>0.75，\n      符合 power curve 预测。这不削弱 C2——反而精确标定了 Blindspot 的 boundary condition：\n      Likert 在 BT<0.75 时 effectively blind（14/14 cells），在 BT>0.75 时偶尔检测到（2/4 cells）。\n      实践指导更清晰：如果你用 Likert 评估 LLM judge bias，你只能发现最极端的偏差，而 moderate 但 \n      practically significant 的 bias 会完全逃过检测。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite (same style)。量化 original \n      preference confound。扩展到 ALL judge×benchmark 组合。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_bt: 0.565\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.085\n      qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_bt: 0.540\n      qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.22\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_bt: 0.555\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.14\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_bt: 0.575\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.052\n      alpacaeval_mean_orig_pref_bt: 0.580\n      alpacaeval_mean_orig_pref_p: 0.06\n      mtbench_mean_orig_pref_bt: 0.550\n      mtbench_mean_orig_pref_p: 0.18\n      cross_judge_orig_pref_heterogeneity_p: 0.65\n      orig_pref_confound_magnitude: \"small (BT 0.54-0.58)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有证据显示 original preference 存在但弱于 style effect：exp-014 GEE originality OR=1.82 p=0.052（marginal），\n      direction analysis 中 casual→formal win rate 54.5%（接近 chance）。Best 档下 RATE control \n      应确认 original preference 是 real but small confound（BT 0.54-0.58），远小于 style effect\n      （BT 0.63-0.77）。这支持 GEE decomposition 的 validity——style 和 originality effects 确实可分离，\n      且 GEE 的 OR estimates 与 RATE control 的 magnitude 一致。Gemini 略高（0.575）因为 Google \n      models 可能对 text naturalness/fluency 更敏感。跨 judge 无异质性（p>0.60），说明 original \n      preference 也是 systematic property。关键：confound 存在但不解释 style effect 的 majority——\n      即使 worst case correction，style BT 仍显著 >0.50。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RATE Control: Original Preference Magnitude by Judge\"\n        columns: [Judge, BT_Orig_Pref, \"95%_CI\", p_value, \"Style_BT_(for_comparison)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 0.565, \"[0.485, 0.645]\", 0.085, 0.630]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 0.540, \"[0.460, 0.620]\", 0.22, 0.665]\n          - [Claude, 0.555, \"[0.475, 0.635]\", 0.14, 0.645]\n          - [Gemini, 0.575, \"[0.495, 0.655]\", 0.052, 0.680]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: style effect BT vs original preference BT for each judge, with CI error bars\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference BT (0.54-0.58) consistently 小于 style effect BT (0.63-0.68) across all judges。\n      差值 0.07-0.12 说明 style manipulation 贡献了大部分 observed effect。GEE decomposition \n      的 formal OR (2.21-4.20) vs originality OR (1.82-4.70) 与 RATE control 的 magnitude ordering 一致，\n      cross-validates 两种 decomposition 方法。Reviewer 担心的 \"style effect is just original preference\"\n      被 quantitatively refuted。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 primary formality experiment 从 n=100 扩展到 n=400。在 exp-001/002 中表现最好的 \n      judge×benchmark 组合上运行。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      n_nli_pass: 348\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.87\n      bt_win_prob: 0.648\n      bt_ci: [0.605, 0.691]\n      bt_p: \"<1e-6\"\n      ci_width: 0.086\n      likert_ate: 0.038\n      likert_p: 0.185\n      likert_tie_rate: 0.61\n      binarized_likert_p: 0.042\n      power_at_observed_effect: 0.99\n      mde_at_80_power: 0.055\n    result_rationale: >\n      n=100 时 BT CI width ~0.15 (e.g., [0.558, 0.703])。n=400 时 CI width 按 √(n) 缩放，\n      预期 ~0.086，giving [0.605, 0.691]。Point estimate 略向 0.50 回归（0.648 vs 0.630）是 \n      典型的 regression to mean effect——n=100 的 estimate 可能轻微 overestimate 因为 winner's curse。\n      关键发现：即使 n=400，Likert ATE 仍然非显著（p=0.185），因为 Likert 的 insensitivity 不是 \n      sample size 问题而是 measurement structure 问题——tie rate ~61% 消耗了大部分 information。\n      但 binarized Likert 在 n=400 时刚好跨过显著性门槛（p=0.042），与 power curve 预测的 n≈462 \n      一致（n=400 power ~0.72，接近但略低于 0.80）。这精确验证了 power curve analysis 的 prediction，\n      是 C2 最强的定量支撑。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Scaled Replication: n=100 vs n=400 Comparison\"\n        columns: [Metric, \"n=100\", \"n=400\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [BT_Win_Prob, 0.630, 0.648, \"Consistent, tighter CI\"]\n          - [BT_CI_Width, 0.145, 0.086, \"√n scaling confirmed\"]\n          - [BT_p, \"<0.001\", \"<1e-6\", \"Both highly significant\"]\n          - [Likert_ATE, 0.056, 0.038, \"Still NS (p=0.185)\"]\n          - [Binarized_Likert_p, 0.296, 0.042, \"Marginal at n=400 — power curve validated\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Power curve overlay: theoretical prediction vs observed detection at n=100 and n=400\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scaled replication 的 triple function：(1) 确认 effect size 的 stability（point estimate \n      within original CI），(2) 证明 Likert insensitivity 不是 underpowered artifact——即使 4x 样本仍 NS，\n      (3) power curve prediction 的 empirical validation（binarized Likert at n=400 marginal，\n      与 n≈462 prediction 高度一致）。这是 C2 从 observation 升级为 quantitative theory 的关键证据。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o register scoring (from QUEUED verification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API scoring on 已验证的 100 register counterfactual pairs（NLI 94% pass）。\n      Pairwise + Likert + GEE decomposition。Exploratory cell，预期 originality-dominated。\n    expected_results:\n      bt_win_prob: 0.585\n      bt_ci: [0.505, 0.665]\n      bt_p: 0.042\n      sign_test_p: 0.085\n      likert_ate: 0.045\n      likert_p: 0.612\n      likert_tie_rate: 0.65\n      gee_academic_or: 1.75\n      gee_academic_p: 0.072\n      gee_originality_or: 4.15\n      gee_originality_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      consistency_rate: 0.58\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3-32B register 结果已显示 originality-dominated pattern（academic OR=1.91 p=0.046, \n      originality OR=5.72 p<0.0001）。GPT-4o 预期相同 pattern 但 effect size 略低——GPT-4o \n      在 formality 上已显示比 Qwen 更弱的 bias（BT 0.63 vs 0.665），register 更弱的 axis \n      在 GPT-4o 上可能仅 marginally significant。BT 0.585 刚过 0.50 显著线（p=0.042），但 \n      sign test 因 consistency_rate 低（0.58）导致 power loss 而 NS（p=0.085）。GEE academic \n      OR=1.75 marginally NS（p=0.072），与 Qwen 的 1.91 方向一致但更弱。Originality OR=4.15 \n      strongly significant，确认 register axis 跨 judge 均为 originality-dominated。\n      这支持 confound gradient 的 robustness：register 在两个 judge 上都是 gradient 的 low end。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Register GEE Decomposition: GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B\"\n        columns: [Judge, Academic_OR, Academic_p, Originality_OR, Originality_p, Classification]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 1.75, 0.072, 4.15, \"<0.0001\", \"originality-dominated\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 1.91, 0.046, 5.72, \"<0.0001\", \"originality-dominated\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"GEE coefficient comparison: paired bars for academic_OR and originality_OR across 2 judges\"\n    analysis: >\n      Register axis 在两个 judge 上一致表现为 originality-dominated（style OR ~1.8-1.9, originality OR ~4-6）。\n      这是 confound gradient 的 anchor point——与 verbosity 的 confound-free（style OR=13.1, originality NS）\n      和 formality 的 mixed（both OR ~2-5）形成清晰的三级梯度。作为 exploratory cell 标注。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为替代 rewriter，在 formality axis 上生成 100 对 counterfactuals。\n      比较 NLI pass rate 和下游 pairwise 结果与 Qwen3-32B 生成的 counterfactuals。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.84\n      llama_bertscore_mean: 0.875\n      llama_pairwise_bt_gpt4o: 0.620\n      llama_pairwise_bt_gpt4o_p: 0.006\n      llama_pairwise_bt_qwen: 0.640\n      llama_pairwise_bt_qwen_p: 0.002\n      qwen_vs_llama_bt_diff: 0.025\n      qwen_vs_llama_diff_p: 0.58\n      cf_quality_comparison_nli_ttest_p: 0.31\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3-32B NLI pass rate 0.88。Llama-3.1-70B 作为同级别 instruction-tuned model，\n      counterfactual generation quality 预期相当（NLI 0.84，略低因为 Llama 的 instruction following \n      在 style transformation 任务上可能略逊于 Qwen3 的 thinking mode）。下游 pairwise 结果\n      差异小且非显著（BT diff ~0.025, p>0.50），因为 judge bias 是 judge 的 property 而非 \n      rewriter 的 property——只要 counterfactual quality 达标（NLI>0.80），不同 rewriter \n      产生的 style manipulation 对 judge 行为的 trigger 效果相同。这 rules out \"Qwen-family \n      artifacts\" concern：bias detection 不依赖于特定 rewriter。P2 priority 但对 robustness \n      narrative 有价值。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Rewriter Comparison: Qwen3-32B vs Llama-3.1-70B\"\n        columns: [Metric, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.1-70B, Diff_p]\n        rows:\n          - [NLI_Pass_Rate, 0.88, 0.84, 0.31]\n          - [BT_GPT4o, 0.630, 0.620, 0.58]\n          - [BT_Qwen, 0.665, 0.640, 0.42]\n          - [Mean_BERTScore, 0.895, 0.875, 0.18]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter identity 对下游 bias detection 无显著影响（all diff p>0.18）。Counterfactual quality \n      有小幅差异（NLI 0.88 vs 0.84）但在 threshold 之上，不影响结论。这是 clean robustness check，\n      一句话写入 paper：results replicate with non-Qwen rewriter (Llama-3.1-70B, BT diff <0.03, p>0.40)。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE + register GEE (API scoring)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API 补齐 verbosity Likert ATE（6/6 Blindspot matrix 的最后一个 cell）和 register \n      GEE decomposition。Verbosity pairwise 已有（86.3% p<10⁻⁶），只缺 Likert。\n    expected_results:\n      verbosity_likert_ate: -0.095\n      verbosity_likert_p: 0.358\n      verbosity_likert_tie_rate: 0.56\n      verbosity_likert_cohens_d: -0.092\n      verbosity_blindspot_confirmed: true\n      blindspot_matrix_complete: \"6/6\"\n      verbosity_gee_verbose_or: 10.5\n      verbosity_gee_verbose_p: \"<1e-7\"\n      verbosity_gee_originality_or: 0.62\n      verbosity_gee_originality_p: 0.22\n      register_bt: 0.585\n      register_bt_p: 0.042\n      register_gee_academic_or: 1.75\n      register_gee_originality_or: 4.15\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 best 档的核心假设之一：GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE 非显著。已有 pairwise 86.3% \n      （最强 bias signal），但 Likert 预期仍然 NS 因为：(1) GPT-4o 的 Likert scoring 在 formality \n      上已显示 tie rate 62.5%，verbosity 的 tie rate 预期略低（56%）但仍 high enough to kill power；\n      (2) ATE 方向可能为负（-0.095）——verbose text 在 Likert absolute scoring 中可能反而被轻微 \n      penalized（\"too wordy\"），而在 pairwise forced comparison 中 overwhelming preferred。这种 \n      sign reversal 是 Blindspot 最强的证据形式：不仅是 \"Likert 看不到\"，而是 \"Likert 看到的方向 \n      都是错的\"。GEE decomposition 预期与 Qwen 一致：verbose OR~10.5 strongly significant，\n      originality NS——确认 verbosity 跨 judge 均为 confound-free pure style bias。\n      完成此实验后 Blindspot evidence matrix 6/6 完整：GPT-4o (formality ✅, verbosity ✅, register ✅) + \n      Qwen3-32B (formality ✅, verbosity ✅, register [exploratory])。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Complete 2×3 Blindspot Evidence Matrix\"\n        columns: [Axis, GPT-4o_BT, GPT-4o_Likert_p, GPT-4o_Blind, Qwen_BT, Qwen_Likert_p, Qwen_Blind]\n        rows:\n          - [Formality, 0.630, 0.332, \"✅\", 0.665, 0.908, \"✅\"]\n          - [Verbosity, 0.863, 0.358, \"✅\", 0.773, 0.179, \"✅\"]\n          - [Register, 0.585, 0.612, \"✅*\", 0.593, 0.505, \"✅*\"]\n      - title: \"Cross-Judge GEE Confound Gradient\"\n        columns: [Axis, GPT-4o_Style_OR, GPT-4o_Orig_OR, Qwen_Style_OR, Qwen_Orig_OR, Classification]\n        rows:\n          - [Verbosity, 10.5, \"0.62 (NS)\", 13.10, \"0.49 (NS)\", confound-free]\n          - [Formality, 2.21, \"1.82 (†)\", 4.20, 4.70, mixed]\n          - [Register, 1.75, 4.15, 1.91, 5.72, originality-dominated]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot (Figure 3): 2 judges × 3 axes BT win prob with 95% CI. Verbosity top, register bottom. Clear gradient visible.\"\n      - \"GEE gradient visualization: stacked bar or slope chart showing style_OR vs originality_OR across 3 axes, 2 judges\"\n    analysis: >\n      6/6 Blindspot matrix 完整。GEE confound gradient 跨 judge 复现：verbosity (pure style, OR>10, \n      originality NS) > formality (mixed, both OR 2-5) > register (originality-dominated, orig OR>4, \n      style OR~2 marginal)。这个 gradient 的 interpretation 是 paper 的 main novelty：axes 的 \n      语义性质决定了 style bias 的 confound structure。Content-preserving axes (verbosity, formality) \n      允许 clean style bias detection；content-altering axes (register, tone) 引入 originality confound \n      甚至 structural incompatibility。这不仅是 empirical observation，而是 practitioner guidance——\n      future work 评估 LLM judge bias 时，axis selection 和 confound decomposition 是必要步骤。\n      GEE decomposition 方法本身是独立 method contribution，超越 \"domain transfer of known phenomenon\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22664,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22664},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"acb706d8-a193-4709-8b02-07580c8d8445","uuid":"8edb109a-3604-4c26-bc36-0b66490141b5"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":188979,"duration_api_ms":190784,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  全部剩余 P0 实验确认 + 写作修复完全解决 R1 审稿意见 + GEE decomposition gradient 被认可为独立方法贡献 → Main 可争。\n  叙事重心从 \"domain transfer of known phenomenon\" 转向 \"first systematic decomposition of style-vs-originality confound structure in LLM judges\"。\n  GEE gradient 作为 main novelty，Blindspot 作为 enabling discovery。6/6 Blindspot matrix 完整，≥3 judges 跨模型验证，\n  confound gradient 跨 judge 复现。Expected review score 3.5-4.0。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude-3.5-Sonnet + Gemini-2.0-Flash)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。使用已有的 100 对 formality counterfactuals，\n      双向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。每个 judge ~400 API 调用。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_bt_win_prob: 0.645\n      claude_bt_ci: [0.565, 0.725]\n      claude_bt_p: 0.0008\n      claude_consistency_rate: 0.62\n      claude_likert_ate: 0.035\n      claude_likert_p: 0.641\n      claude_likert_tie_rate: 0.59\n      gemini_bt_win_prob: 0.680\n      gemini_bt_ci: [0.595, 0.755]\n      gemini_bt_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      gemini_consistency_rate: 0.67\n      gemini_likert_ate: -0.022\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.782\n      gemini_likert_tie_rate: 0.64\n      blindspot_confirmed_claude: true\n      blindspot_confirmed_gemini: true\n      total_judges_with_blindspot: 4\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o BT 63.0% 和 Qwen3-32B BT 66.5% 已建立 formality bias 的跨模型基线。Best 档下，Claude 和 Gemini \n      作为 instruction-tuned LLM judges 共享相同的 RLHF training signal（偏好 formal/polished 输出），因此预期 \n      BT win prob 落在 0.60-0.70 区间。Claude 略保守（0.645）因为 Anthropic 的 constitutional AI training \n      可能部分缓解 surface-level style preference；Gemini 略高（0.680）因为 Google 的 training pipeline \n      更强调 helpfulness/polish。Likert ATE 在两个 judge 上均非显著，因为 Likert 的 absolute scoring \n      结构性缺陷（high tie rate ~60%+）与 judge 身份无关——这是测量方法本身的问题。这给出 4 个 judge 全部确认 \n      Blindspot，远超核心假设要求的 ≥3 judges。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Judge Formality BT Win Probabilities\"\n        columns: [Judge, BT_Win_Prob, \"95%_CI\", p_value, Likert_ATE, Likert_p, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 0.630, \"[0.558, 0.703]\", \"<0.001\", 0.056, 0.332, \"✅\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 0.665, \"[0.585, 0.739]\", \"<0.0001\", 0.011, 0.908, \"✅\"]\n          - [Claude-3.5-Sonnet, 0.645, \"[0.565, 0.725]\", 0.0008, 0.035, 0.641, \"✅\"]\n          - [Gemini-2.0-Flash, 0.680, \"[0.595, 0.755]\", \"<0.0001\", -0.022, 0.782, \"✅\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot panel: 4 judges formality BT win prob with 95% CI, horizontal dashed line at 0.50\"\n    analysis: >\n      4/4 judges 在 pairwise 上显著检测 formality bias（all p<0.001），而 4/4 judges 在 Likert 上非显著\n      （all p>0.30）。Effect size 跨 judge 一致（BT 0.63-0.68），方差小，说明 formality bias 是 LLM judge \n      的 systematic property 而非个别模型 quirk。Likert tie rate 跨 judge 均 >0.55，这是 Blindspot \n      的机制根源。Cochran's Q test for heterogeneity 预期 p>0.30（同质性）。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (AlpacaEval + MT-Bench)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新的 counterfactual generation\n      （不同 source text）。每个 benchmark 100 对，3 judges (GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini) scoring。\n    expected_results:\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_bt: 0.615\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.005\n      alpacaeval_claude_bt: 0.625\n      alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.003\n      alpacaeval_gemini_bt: 0.650\n      alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.0005\n      mtbench_gpt4o_bt: 0.590\n      mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.025\n      mtbench_claude_bt: 0.610\n      mtbench_claude_p: 0.009\n      mtbench_gemini_bt: 0.640\n      mtbench_gemini_p: 0.001\n      nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.85\n      nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.82\n      cross_benchmark_heterogeneity_p: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      AlpacaEval 源文本更长更开放（instruction-following），counterfactual quality 预期与 LLMBar 相当\n      （NLI ~0.85），effect size 略低于 LLMBar 因为 AlpacaEval 文本的 stylistic variance 更大，\n      稀释 formality manipulation 的 relative salience。MT-Bench 文本更短更结构化（multi-turn QA），\n      effect size 进一步降低（BT ~0.59-0.64）因为短文本中 formality shift 的 perceptual impact 更小，\n      且 MT-Bench 的 evaluation criteria 更偏向 correctness/helpfulness。但所有 cells 仍在 best 档\n      指标范围内（BT 0.60-0.85）。效应方向一致（formal preferred），跨 benchmark 无异质性\n      （Cochran's Q p>0.40），支持 generalizability claim。NLI pass rate 在新 benchmark 上略低\n      （0.82-0.85 vs LLMBar 0.88）因为不同 domain text 的 counterfactual generation 难度略有差异。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Benchmark × Cross-Judge BT Win Probabilities (Formality)\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini]\n        rows:\n          - [LLMBar, \"0.630*\", \"0.645*\", \"0.680*\"]\n          - [AlpacaEval, \"0.615*\", \"0.625*\", \"0.650*\"]\n          - [MT-Bench, \"0.590*\", \"0.610*\", \"0.640*\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3 benchmarks × 3 judges, color-coded BT win prob, all cells annotated with significance stars\"\n    analysis: >\n      9/9 benchmark×judge cells 均在 pairwise 上显著（all p<0.05），effect size 0.59-0.68。\n      Benchmark 间差异小（mean BT across judges: LLMBar 0.652, AlpacaEval 0.630, MT-Bench 0.613），\n      说明 formality bias 不依赖于特定 benchmark 的 text distribution。Judge 间方差也小（within-benchmark SD ~0.03）。\n      这为 C1（pipeline generalizability）和 C3（effect robustness）提供强证据。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across all judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 judge×benchmark×axis 组合，在同一 counterfactual data 上计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise BT win rate。\n      系统性比较测量敏感度。如果 Likert 在某些 cell 检测到强效应（如 verbosity），C2 需约束为 \n      \"Likert fails on weak-to-moderate signals\"。\n    expected_results:\n      total_cells_tested: 18\n      pairwise_significant_cells: 16\n      likert_significant_cells: 2\n      blindspot_rate: 0.875\n      likert_detects_verbosity_gemini: true\n      likert_verbosity_gemini_ate: 0.28\n      likert_verbosity_gemini_p: 0.038\n      likert_detects_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval: true\n      likert_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval_ate: 0.31\n      likert_verbosity_qwen_alpacaeval_p: 0.029\n      mean_pairwise_bt: 0.665\n      mean_likert_ate: 0.042\n      sensitivity_ratio_median: 4.8\n      power_curve_crossover_n: 450\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下 Blindspot 确认率 ≥83%，预期 16/18 cells（89%）pairwise 显著但 Likert 非显著。\n      2 个 Likert 显著 cell 出现在 verbosity axis 上——verbosity 是 effect size 最大的 axis\n      （Qwen BT 77.3%，GPT-4o pairwise 86.3%），在极端 effect size 下 Likert 的 tie rate 降低\n      （verbosity Qwen tie rate 58.1% vs formality 72.7%），少数 judge×benchmark 组合刚好跨过\n      显著性门槛。这实际上 *strengthens* C2 framing：Likert 只在最极端的 bias 下才勉强检测到，\n      而 pairwise 在所有 moderate-to-strong effects 上均显著。Power curve 显示 Likert 在 \n      typical n=100 样本量下需要 BT>0.75 才可能达到 p<0.05，与经验数据一致。\n      C2 的 refined statement：Likert 在 moderate effect sizes (BT 0.60-0.70) 上 systematically blind，\n      仅在 extreme effects (BT>0.75) 上偶尔检测到——但 pairwise 在所有水平上均敏感。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Likert vs Pairwise Detection Matrix (p<0.05)\"\n        columns: [Cell, Pairwise_BT, Pairwise_p, Likert_ATE, Likert_p, Blindspot]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar × Formality\", 0.630, \"<0.001\", 0.056, 0.332, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"Qwen × LLMBar × Formality\", 0.665, \"<0.0001\", 0.011, 0.908, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar × Formality\", 0.645, 0.0008, 0.035, 0.641, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar × Formality\", 0.680, \"<0.0001\", -0.022, 0.782, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar × Verbosity\", 0.863, \"<1e-6\", 0.082, 0.418, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"Qwen × LLMBar × Verbosity\", 0.773, \"<0.0001\", -0.151, 0.179, \"✅\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar × Verbosity\", 0.755, \"<0.0001\", 0.280, 0.038, \"❌\"]\n          - [\"... (14 more cells)\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\", \"...\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: x=BT win prob, y=Likert |ATE|, color=significant/NS, with detection threshold curves for both methods\"\n      - \"Power curve comparison: BT vs binarized Likert, annotated with observed cell positions\"\n    analysis: >\n      Sensitivity ratio (pairwise effect / Likert effect) median 4.8x，说明 pairwise 的 measurement \n      resolution 系统性高于 Likert。2 个 Likert-detectable cells 均在 verbosity axis 且 BT>0.75，\n      符合 power curve 预测。这不削弱 C2——反而精确标定了 Blindspot 的 boundary condition：\n      Likert 在 BT<0.75 时 effectively blind（14/14 cells），在 BT>0.75 时偶尔检测到（2/4 cells）。\n      实践指导更清晰：如果你用 Likert 评估 LLM judge bias，你只能发现最极端的偏差，而 moderate 但 \n      practically significant 的 bias 会完全逃过检测。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite (same style)。量化 original \n      preference confound。扩展到 ALL judge×benchmark 组合。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_bt: 0.565\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.085\n      qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_bt: 0.540\n      qwen_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.22\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_bt: 0.555\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.14\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_bt: 0.575\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.052\n      alpacaeval_mean_orig_pref_bt: 0.580\n      alpacaeval_mean_orig_pref_p: 0.06\n      mtbench_mean_orig_pref_bt: 0.550\n      mtbench_mean_orig_pref_p: 0.18\n      cross_judge_orig_pref_heterogeneity_p: 0.65\n      orig_pref_confound_magnitude: \"small (BT 0.54-0.58)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有证据显示 original preference 存在但弱于 style effect：exp-014 GEE originality OR=1.82 p=0.052（marginal），\n      direction analysis 中 casual→formal win rate 54.5%（接近 chance）。Best 档下 RATE control \n      应确认 original preference 是 real but small confound（BT 0.54-0.58），远小于 style effect\n      （BT 0.63-0.77）。这支持 GEE decomposition 的 validity——style 和 originality effects 确实可分离，\n      且 GEE 的 OR estimates 与 RATE control 的 magnitude 一致。Gemini 略高（0.575）因为 Google \n      models 可能对 text naturalness/fluency 更敏感。跨 judge 无异质性（p>0.60），说明 original \n      preference 也是 systematic property。关键：confound 存在但不解释 style effect 的 majority——\n      即使 worst case correction，style BT 仍显著 >0.50。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"RATE Control: Original Preference Magnitude by Judge\"\n        columns: [Judge, BT_Orig_Pref, \"95%_CI\", p_value, \"Style_BT_(for_comparison)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 0.565, \"[0.485, 0.645]\", 0.085, 0.630]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 0.540, \"[0.460, 0.620]\", 0.22, 0.665]\n          - [Claude, 0.555, \"[0.475, 0.635]\", 0.14, 0.645]\n          - [Gemini, 0.575, \"[0.495, 0.655]\", 0.052, 0.680]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: style effect BT vs original preference BT for each judge, with CI error bars\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference BT (0.54-0.58) consistently 小于 style effect BT (0.63-0.68) across all judges。\n      差值 0.07-0.12 说明 style manipulation 贡献了大部分 observed effect。GEE decomposition \n      的 formal OR (2.21-4.20) vs originality OR (1.82-4.70) 与 RATE control 的 magnitude ordering 一致，\n      cross-validates 两种 decomposition 方法。Reviewer 担心的 \"style effect is just original preference\"\n      被 quantitatively refuted。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 primary formality experiment 从 n=100 扩展到 n=400。在 exp-001/002 中表现最好的 \n      judge×benchmark 组合上运行。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      n_nli_pass: 348\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.87\n      bt_win_prob: 0.648\n      bt_ci: [0.605, 0.691]\n      bt_p: \"<1e-6\"\n      ci_width: 0.086\n      likert_ate: 0.038\n      likert_p: 0.185\n      likert_tie_rate: 0.61\n      binarized_likert_p: 0.042\n      power_at_observed_effect: 0.99\n      mde_at_80_power: 0.055\n    result_rationale: >\n      n=100 时 BT CI width ~0.15 (e.g., [0.558, 0.703])。n=400 时 CI width 按 √(n) 缩放，\n      预期 ~0.086，giving [0.605, 0.691]。Point estimate 略向 0.50 回归（0.648 vs 0.630）是 \n      典型的 regression to mean effect——n=100 的 estimate 可能轻微 overestimate 因为 winner's curse。\n      关键发现：即使 n=400，Likert ATE 仍然非显著（p=0.185），因为 Likert 的 insensitivity 不是 \n      sample size 问题而是 measurement structure 问题——tie rate ~61% 消耗了大部分 information。\n      但 binarized Likert 在 n=400 时刚好跨过显著性门槛（p=0.042），与 power curve 预测的 n≈462 \n      一致（n=400 power ~0.72，接近但略低于 0.80）。这精确验证了 power curve analysis 的 prediction，\n      是 C2 最强的定量支撑。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Scaled Replication: n=100 vs n=400 Comparison\"\n        columns: [Metric, \"n=100\", \"n=400\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [BT_Win_Prob, 0.630, 0.648, \"Consistent, tighter CI\"]\n          - [BT_CI_Width, 0.145, 0.086, \"√n scaling confirmed\"]\n          - [BT_p, \"<0.001\", \"<1e-6\", \"Both highly significant\"]\n          - [Likert_ATE, 0.056, 0.038, \"Still NS (p=0.185)\"]\n          - [Binarized_Likert_p, 0.296, 0.042, \"Marginal at n=400 — power curve validated\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Power curve overlay: theoretical prediction vs observed detection at n=100 and n=400\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scaled replication 的 triple function：(1) 确认 effect size 的 stability（point estimate \n      within original CI），(2) 证明 Likert insensitivity 不是 underpowered artifact——即使 4x 样本仍 NS，\n      (3) power curve prediction 的 empirical validation（binarized Likert at n=400 marginal，\n      与 n≈462 prediction 高度一致）。这是 C2 从 observation 升级为 quantitative theory 的关键证据。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o register scoring (from QUEUED verification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API scoring on 已验证的 100 register counterfactual pairs（NLI 94% pass）。\n      Pairwise + Likert + GEE decomposition。Exploratory cell，预期 originality-dominated。\n    expected_results:\n      bt_win_prob: 0.585\n      bt_ci: [0.505, 0.665]\n      bt_p: 0.042\n      sign_test_p: 0.085\n      likert_ate: 0.045\n      likert_p: 0.612\n      likert_tie_rate: 0.65\n      gee_academic_or: 1.75\n      gee_academic_p: 0.072\n      gee_originality_or: 4.15\n      gee_originality_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      consistency_rate: 0.58\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3-32B register 结果已显示 originality-dominated pattern（academic OR=1.91 p=0.046, \n      originality OR=5.72 p<0.0001）。GPT-4o 预期相同 pattern 但 effect size 略低——GPT-4o \n      在 formality 上已显示比 Qwen 更弱的 bias（BT 0.63 vs 0.665），register 更弱的 axis \n      在 GPT-4o 上可能仅 marginally significant。BT 0.585 刚过 0.50 显著线（p=0.042），但 \n      sign test 因 consistency_rate 低（0.58）导致 power loss 而 NS（p=0.085）。GEE academic \n      OR=1.75 marginally NS（p=0.072），与 Qwen 的 1.91 方向一致但更弱。Originality OR=4.15 \n      strongly significant，确认 register axis 跨 judge 均为 originality-dominated。\n      这支持 confound gradient 的 robustness：register 在两个 judge 上都是 gradient 的 low end。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Register GEE Decomposition: GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B\"\n        columns: [Judge, Academic_OR, Academic_p, Originality_OR, Originality_p, Classification]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 1.75, 0.072, 4.15, \"<0.0001\", \"originality-dominated\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, 1.91, 0.046, 5.72, \"<0.0001\", \"originality-dominated\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"GEE coefficient comparison: paired bars for academic_OR and originality_OR across 2 judges\"\n    analysis: >\n      Register axis 在两个 judge 上一致表现为 originality-dominated（style OR ~1.8-1.9, originality OR ~4-6）。\n      这是 confound gradient 的 anchor point——与 verbosity 的 confound-free（style OR=13.1, originality NS）\n      和 formality 的 mixed（both OR ~2-5）形成清晰的三级梯度。作为 exploratory cell 标注。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为替代 rewriter，在 formality axis 上生成 100 对 counterfactuals。\n      比较 NLI pass rate 和下游 pairwise 结果与 Qwen3-32B 生成的 counterfactuals。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.84\n      llama_bertscore_mean: 0.875\n      llama_pairwise_bt_gpt4o: 0.620\n      llama_pairwise_bt_gpt4o_p: 0.006\n      llama_pairwise_bt_qwen: 0.640\n      llama_pairwise_bt_qwen_p: 0.002\n      qwen_vs_llama_bt_diff: 0.025\n      qwen_vs_llama_diff_p: 0.58\n      cf_quality_comparison_nli_ttest_p: 0.31\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3-32B NLI pass rate 0.88。Llama-3.1-70B 作为同级别 instruction-tuned model，\n      counterfactual generation quality 预期相当（NLI 0.84，略低因为 Llama 的 instruction following \n      在 style transformation 任务上可能略逊于 Qwen3 的 thinking mode）。下游 pairwise 结果\n      差异小且非显著（BT diff ~0.025, p>0.50），因为 judge bias 是 judge 的 property 而非 \n      rewriter 的 property——只要 counterfactual quality 达标（NLI>0.80），不同 rewriter \n      产生的 style manipulation 对 judge 行为的 trigger 效果相同。这 rules out \"Qwen-family \n      artifacts\" concern：bias detection 不依赖于特定 rewriter。P2 priority 但对 robustness \n      narrative 有价值。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Rewriter Comparison: Qwen3-32B vs Llama-3.1-70B\"\n        columns: [Metric, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.1-70B, Diff_p]\n        rows:\n          - [NLI_Pass_Rate, 0.88, 0.84, 0.31]\n          - [BT_GPT4o, 0.630, 0.620, 0.58]\n          - [BT_Qwen, 0.665, 0.640, 0.42]\n          - [Mean_BERTScore, 0.895, 0.875, 0.18]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter identity 对下游 bias detection 无显著影响（all diff p>0.18）。Counterfactual quality \n      有小幅差异（NLI 0.88 vs 0.84）但在 threshold 之上，不影响结论。这是 clean robustness check，\n      一句话写入 paper：results replicate with non-Qwen rewriter (Llama-3.1-70B, BT diff <0.03, p>0.40)。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE + register GEE (API scoring)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API 补齐 verbosity Likert ATE（6/6 Blindspot matrix 的最后一个 cell）和 register \n      GEE decomposition。Verbosity pairwise 已有（86.3% p<10⁻⁶），只缺 Likert。\n    expected_results:\n      verbosity_likert_ate: -0.095\n      verbosity_likert_p: 0.358\n      verbosity_likert_tie_rate: 0.56\n      verbosity_likert_cohens_d: -0.092\n      verbosity_blindspot_confirmed: true\n      blindspot_matrix_complete: \"6/6\"\n      verbosity_gee_verbose_or: 10.5\n      verbosity_gee_verbose_p: \"<1e-7\"\n      verbosity_gee_originality_or: 0.62\n      verbosity_gee_originality_p: 0.22\n      register_bt: 0.585\n      register_bt_p: 0.042\n      register_gee_academic_or: 1.75\n      register_gee_originality_or: 4.15\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 best 档的核心假设之一：GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE 非显著。已有 pairwise 86.3% \n      （最强 bias signal），但 Likert 预期仍然 NS 因为：(1) GPT-4o 的 Likert scoring 在 formality \n      上已显示 tie rate 62.5%，verbosity 的 tie rate 预期略低（56%）但仍 high enough to kill power；\n      (2) ATE 方向可能为负（-0.095）——verbose text 在 Likert absolute scoring 中可能反而被轻微 \n      penalized（\"too wordy\"），而在 pairwise forced comparison 中 overwhelming preferred。这种 \n      sign reversal 是 Blindspot 最强的证据形式：不仅是 \"Likert 看不到\"，而是 \"Likert 看到的方向 \n      都是错的\"。GEE decomposition 预期与 Qwen 一致：verbose OR~10.5 strongly significant，\n      originality NS——确认 verbosity 跨 judge 均为 confound-free pure style bias。\n      完成此实验后 Blindspot evidence matrix 6/6 完整：GPT-4o (formality ✅, verbosity ✅, register ✅) + \n      Qwen3-32B (formality ✅, verbosity ✅, register [exploratory])。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Complete 2×3 Blindspot Evidence Matrix\"\n        columns: [Axis, GPT-4o_BT, GPT-4o_Likert_p, GPT-4o_Blind, Qwen_BT, Qwen_Likert_p, Qwen_Blind]\n        rows:\n          - [Formality, 0.630, 0.332, \"✅\", 0.665, 0.908, \"✅\"]\n          - [Verbosity, 0.863, 0.358, \"✅\", 0.773, 0.179, \"✅\"]\n          - [Register, 0.585, 0.612, \"✅*\", 0.593, 0.505, \"✅*\"]\n      - title: \"Cross-Judge GEE Confound Gradient\"\n        columns: [Axis, GPT-4o_Style_OR, GPT-4o_Orig_OR, Qwen_Style_OR, Qwen_Orig_OR, Classification]\n        rows:\n          - [Verbosity, 10.5, \"0.62 (NS)\", 13.10, \"0.49 (NS)\", confound-free]\n          - [Formality, 2.21, \"1.82 (†)\", 4.20, 4.70, mixed]\n          - [Register, 1.75, 4.15, 1.91, 5.72, originality-dominated]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot (Figure 3): 2 judges × 3 axes BT win prob with 95% CI. Verbosity top, register bottom. Clear gradient visible.\"\n      - \"GEE gradient visualization: stacked bar or slope chart showing style_OR vs originality_OR across 3 axes, 2 judges\"\n    analysis: >\n      6/6 Blindspot matrix 完整。GEE confound gradient 跨 judge 复现：verbosity (pure style, OR>10, \n      originality NS) > formality (mixed, both OR 2-5) > register (originality-dominated, orig OR>4, \n      style OR~2 marginal)。这个 gradient 的 interpretation 是 paper 的 main novelty：axes 的 \n      语义性质决定了 style bias 的 confound structure。Content-preserving axes (verbosity, formality) \n      允许 clean style bias detection；content-altering axes (register, tone) 引入 originality confound \n      甚至 structural incompatibility。这不仅是 empirical observation，而是 practitioner guidance——\n      future work 评估 LLM judge bias 时，axis selection 和 confound decomposition 是必要步骤。\n      GEE decomposition 方法本身是独立 method contribution，超越 \"domain transfer of known phenomenon\"。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"acb706d8-a193-4709-8b02-07580c8d8445","total_cost_usd":0.41647750000000006,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22664,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":10047,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22664,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10047,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":22664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":22664},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":17622,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchR